        "explanation": "Senator Landrieu claims casework credit-claiming by stating that she intervened directly with the Department of Homeland Security to remove bureaucratic red tape and secure medical entry to the US for an injured Iraqi child."
      }
    ],
    "negative_clarification": "Do not classify a text as credit-claiming if the senator merely expresses support for a policy, introduces or cosponsors a new bill, details ongoing committee actions, holds hearings, or praises local agencies for securing grants without claiming personal or delegation responsibility for bringing those funds. Symbolic acts, memorials, op-eds, general policy discussions, and criticism of opponents are position-taking or advertising, not credit-claiming.",
    "negative_examples": [
      {
